  "nameStory": "",
  "description": "Powder-scale pholiota is a small, delicate mushroom characterized by its pale yellowish to whitish caps covered in fine, powdery scales. This species belongs to the Tubariaceae family and is commonly found in New England woodlands during moist periods.",
  "idTips": [
    {
      "label": "Powdery Cap Surface",
      "description": "The cap is distinctively covered with fine, powder-like scales that give it a frosted or granular appearance",
      "isPrimary": true
    },
    {
      "label": "Small Size",
      "description": "Caps typically measure 1-3 cm in diameter, making it a miniature species easily overlooked",
      "isPrimary": false
    },
    {
      "label": "Attached Gills",
      "description": "The gills are adnate to slightly decurrent and are pale yellowish, matching the overall pale coloration of the fruiting body",
      "isPrimary": false
    }
  ],
  "habitat": "Powder-scale pholiota grows on mossy wood, bark, and decaying plant debris in moist forests and woodland areas throughout New England.",
